exports[`AU > reads as expected 1`] = `
"Offer of employment: Senior Backend Engineer

Munich, 16 October 2026

Dear Lena,

We are pleased to offer you employment as Senior Backend Engineer in our Platform team with Example Engineering GmbH. This letter sets out the terms of our offer.

## Your role and start date

You will report to Jonas Becker, Engineering Manager. Your employment will begin on 1 December 2026.

## Place of work and hours

You will work at our Munich office, with up to two days of remote work a week. Your ordinary hours of work will be 38 hours a week, plus reasonable additional hours.

## Remuneration

Your base salary will be $78,000 a year, plus superannuation, paid fortnightly.

| Component | Gross amount |
| Annual base salary (without superannuation) | $78,000.00 |
| Each payment (26 a year) | $3,000.00 |

## Annual bonus

You will be eligible for an annual bonus of up to 10% of your annual gross salary, based on targets agreed each year, under the terms of the company’s bonus plan in effect at the time.

## Probation

The first 6 months of your employment will be a probation period. During this time either party may end the employment by giving one week’s notice, or the notice required by the National Employment Standards or an applicable award if that is longer.

## Leave

You will receive 28 days of paid annual leave each year, together with personal/carer’s leave and the other leave in the National Employment Standards.

## Notice periods

After probation, either party may end the employment by giving notice in writing. The company will give you at least the notice required by the National Employment Standards, which depends on your length of service and age.

## Superannuation

The company will make superannuation contributions for you at the rate required by superannuation guarantee law, into the fund you choose. If you don’t choose a fund, we will pay into your existing (stapled) fund or our default fund.

## Benefits

You will also receive a monthly public transport allowance, a company pension contribution and a learning budget of €1,000 a year.

## Relocation support

To help with your move, we will provide a one-off relocation allowance of €3,000 gross.

## Modern award

Your employment is covered by the Professional Employees Award 2020. If anything in this letter is less favourable to you than the award or agreement, the award or agreement applies.

## Information statements

With this letter you will receive the Fair Work Information Statement, which explain your rights at work.

## Conditions of this offer

This offer depends on:

- proof of your right to work in Australia
- references that are satisfactory to the company

Please confirm that you accept this offer by signing and returning a copy of this letter by 30 October 2026. We look forward to working with you.

Yours sincerely,

[For Example Engineering GmbH] [Accepted by the candidate: I accept this offer on the terms set out above.]

Example Engineering GmbH never charges candidates fees."
`;

exports[`CA-AB > reads as expected 1`] = `
"Offer of employment: Senior Backend Engineer

October 16, 2026

Dear Lena,

We are pleased to offer you the position of Senior Backend Engineer in our Platform team at Example Engineering GmbH. This letter sets out the terms of our offer.

## Your role and start date

You will report to Jonas Becker, Engineering Manager. Your employment will begin on December 1, 2026.

## Place of work and hours

You will work at our Munich office, with up to two days of remote work a week. Your regular hours of work will be 40 hours a week.

## Compensation

Your annual salary will be $78,000, paid every two weeks, less the deductions required by law, including income tax, Canada Pension Plan (CPP) contributions and Employment Insurance (EI) premiums.

| Component | Gross amount |
| Annual salary | $78,000.00 |
| Each payment (26 a year) | $3,000.00 |

## Annual bonus

You will be eligible for an annual bonus of up to 10% of your annual gross salary, based on targets agreed each year, under the terms of the company’s bonus plan in effect at the time.

## Probationary period

The first 3 months of your employment will be a probationary period, during which the company will assess your fit for the role.

## Vacation and general holidays

You will receive 28 days of paid vacation a year, and at least the vacation time and vacation pay required by the Employment Standards Code. You will also be entitled to Alberta’s general holidays.

## Ending your employment

If your employment is ended without cause after the probationary period, the company will give you at least the notice or pay in lieu of notice required by the Employment Standards Code.

## Retirement savings

You will be eligible to join the company’s retirement savings plan: a group RRSP with matching contributions of up to 4% of salary.

## Benefits

You will also receive a monthly public transport allowance, a company pension contribution and a learning budget of €1,000 a year.

## Relocation support

To help with your move, we will provide a one-off relocation allowance of €3,000 gross.

## Conditions of this offer

This offer depends on:

- proof that you are legally entitled to work in Canada
- references that are satisfactory to the company

To accept this offer, please sign and return a copy of this letter by October 30, 2026. We look forward to working with you.

Sincerely,

[For Example Engineering GmbH] [Accepted by the candidate: I accept this offer on the terms set out above.]

Example Engineering GmbH never charges candidates fees."
`;

