exports[`DE > reads as expected 1`] = `
"Offer of employment: Senior Backend Engineer

Munich, 16 October 2026

Dear Lena,

We are delighted to offer you the position of Senior Backend Engineer in our Platform team at Example Engineering GmbH. This letter sets out the main terms of our offer. Your employment contract will confirm these and the remaining terms in writing.

## Your role and start date

You will report to Jonas Becker, Engineering Manager. Your employment will begin on 1 December 2026.

## Place of work and hours

Your place of work will be our Munich office, with up to two days of remote work a week. Your regular working time will be 40 hours a week, Monday to Friday.

## Salary

Your annual gross salary will be €78,000, paid in 12 equal instalments at the end of each month.

| Component | Gross amount |
| Annual salary | €78,000.00 |
| Each instalment (12 a year) | €6,500.00 |

## Annual bonus

You will be eligible for an annual bonus of up to 10% of your annual gross salary, based on targets agreed each year. The rules of the bonus scheme in force at the time apply.

## Probation

The first 6 months of your employment are a probation period. During probation, either party may end the employment with two weeks’ notice.

## Holiday

You will receive 28 working days of paid holiday in each calendar year, based on a five-day week. This includes your statutory minimum holiday.

## Notice periods

After probation, the notice periods in section 622 of the German Civil Code (BGB) apply. Any longer notice period that applies to the company also applies to you. Notice must be given in writing.

## Company pension

You may convert part of your salary into a company pension (Entgeltumwandlung) under the Company Pensions Act (BetrAVG). The company adds 20% to the amount you convert.

## Benefits

You will also receive a monthly public transport allowance, a company pension contribution and a learning budget of €1,000 a year.

## Relocation support

To help with your move, we will provide a one-off relocation allowance of €3,000 gross.

## Advice for workers from outside the EU

You can get free and confidential advice about your rights at work in Germany, in several languages, from the counselling service Faire Integration (www.faire-integration.de).

## Written terms of employment

You will receive the written record of your essential terms of employment that the Nachweisgesetz requires with your employment contract.

## Conditions of this offer

This offer depends on:

- proof of your right to work in Germany before your start date
- references that are satisfactory to the company

Please confirm that you accept this offer by signing and returning a copy of this letter by 30 October 2026. We look forward to welcoming you to the team.

Yours sincerely,

[For Example Engineering GmbH] [Accepted by the candidate: I accept this offer on the terms set out above.]

Example Engineering GmbH never charges candidates fees."
`;

