Munich, 16 October 2026

Dear Lena,

We are delighted to offer you the position of Senior Backend Engineer in our Platform team at Example Engineering GmbH. This letter sets out the main terms of our offer. Your employment contract will confirm these and the remaining terms in writing.

## Your role and start date

You will report to Jonas Becker, Engineering Manager. Your employment will begin on 1 December 2026.

## Place of work and hours

Your place of work will be our Munich office, with up to two days of remote work a week. Your working week will be 40 hours.

## Salary

Your gross salary will be €78,000 a year, paid monthly. You will also receive a holiday allowance (vakantiegeld) of at least 8% of your gross salary, paid each year in May.

| Component | Gross amount |
| Annual salary (without holiday allowance) | €78,000.00 |
| Each monthly payment | €6,500.00 |

## Annual bonus

You will be eligible for an annual bonus of up to 10% of your annual gross salary, based on targets agreed each year. The rules of the bonus scheme in force at the time apply.

## Probation

Your employment starts with a probation period (proeftijd) of 2 months, which applies equally to you and the company. During probation, either party may end the employment with immediate effect.

## Holiday and leave

You will receive 28 days of paid holiday a year, based on a full-time working week. The statutory minimum is four times your weekly working hours.

## Notice periods

After probation, if the employment is ended, the statutory notice periods in the Dutch Civil Code apply: one month for you, and one to four months for the company, depending on how long you have worked for us. Notice ends on the last day of a calendar month. Ending the employment is subject to Dutch dismissal law.

## Pension

You will join the company’s pension scheme: the PMT sector pension fund.

## Benefits

You will also receive a monthly public transport allowance, a company pension contribution and a learning budget of €1,000 a year.

## Relocation support

To help with your move, we will provide a one-off relocation allowance of €3,000 gross.

## Collective labour agreement (CAO)

The CAO voor de Metaal en Techniek applies to your employment. Where it gives you better terms than this letter, the collective agreement applies.

## Conditions of this offer

This offer depends on:

- proof of your right to work in the Netherlands, including a residence and work permit if you need one
- references that are satisfactory to the company

Please confirm that you accept this offer by signing and returning a copy of this letter by 30 October 2026. We look forward to welcoming you to the team.

Yours sincerely,

[For Example Engineering GmbH] [Accepted by the candidate: I accept this offer on the terms set out above.]

Example Engineering GmbH never charges candidates fees."
`;

exports[`NZ > reads as expected 1`] = `
"Offer of employment: Senior Backend Engineer

Munich, 16 October 2026

Dear Lena,

We are pleased to offer you the position of Senior Backend Engineer in our Platform team at Example Engineering GmbH. This letter sets out the main terms of our offer. Your individual employment agreement sets out all the terms of your employment.

## Your role and start date

You will report to Jonas Becker, Engineering Manager. Your employment will begin on 1 December 2026.

## Place of work and hours

You will work at our Munich office, with up to two days of remote work a week. Your hours of work will be 40 hours a week.

## Salary

Your salary will be $78,000 a year, paid fortnightly.

| Component | Gross amount |
| Annual salary | $78,000.00 |
| Each payment (26 a year) | $3,000.00 |

## Annual bonus

You will be eligible for an annual bonus of up to 10% of your annual gross salary, based on targets agreed each year, under the terms of the company’s bonus scheme in force at the time.

## Trial period

Your employment is subject to a trial period of 90 days from your start date, under sections 67A and 67B of the Employment Relations Act 2000. If the company ends your employment during the trial period by giving notice, you will not be able to raise a personal grievance for unjustified dismissal. You keep your other rights, including the right to raise a personal grievance on other grounds.

## Holidays and leave

You will receive 28 days of paid annual holidays a year, as well as public holidays, sick leave and the other leave in the Holidays Act 2003.

## Notice periods

Either party may end the employment by giving four weeks’ notice in writing.

## KiwiSaver

If you are eligible, you will be automatically enrolled in KiwiSaver when you start, and you can choose to opt out. The company will make at least the compulsory employer contributions.

## Benefits

You will also receive a monthly public transport allowance, a company pension contribution and a learning budget of €1,000 a year.

## Relocation support

To help with your move, we will provide a one-off relocation allowance of €3,000 gross.

## Your right to seek advice

You are entitled to seek independent advice about this offer and the employment agreement, and we will give you reasonable time to do so before you accept.

## Employment agreement

Your employment will be under a written individual employment agreement, which we will give you with this letter. It explains how employment relationship problems can be resolved, including the 90 days within which a personal grievance must be raised.

## Conditions of this offer

This offer depends on:

- proof of your right to work in New Zealand, including a work visa if you need one
- references that are satisfactory to the company

Please confirm that you accept this offer by signing and returning a copy of this letter and the employment agreement by 30 October 2026. We look forward to working with you.

Yours sincerely,

[For Example Engineering GmbH] [Accepted by the candidate: I accept this offer on the terms set out above.]

Example Engineering GmbH never charges candidates fees."
`;

exports[`US > reads as expected 1`] = `
"Offer of employment: Senior Backend Engineer

October 16, 2026

Dear Lena,

We are pleased to offer you the position of Senior Backend Engineer in our Platform team at Example Engineering GmbH. This letter sets out the terms of our offer.

## Your role and start date

You will report to Jonas Becker, Engineering Manager. Your first day of work will be December 1, 2026.

## Place of work

You will work at our Munich office, with up to two days of remote work a week, normally 40 hours a week.

## Compensation

Your starting salary will be $78,000 a year, paid twice a month under the company’s normal payroll practices.

| Component | Gross amount |
| Annual base salary | $78,000.00 |
| Each payment (24 a year) | $3,250.00 |

## Overtime status

This position is classified as non-exempt under the Fair Labor Standards Act, which means you will be paid for overtime in line with federal and state law.

## Annual bonus

You will be eligible for an annual bonus of up to 10% of your annual gross salary, based on targets agreed each year, under the terms of the company’s bonus plan in effect at the time.

## Paid time off

You will receive 28 days of paid time off each year, under the company’s time-off policy.

## Benefits

You will be eligible to take part in the company’s benefit plans, including a monthly public transport allowance, a company pension contribution and a learning budget of €1,000 a year, under the terms of each plan.

## Relocation support

To help with your move, we will provide a one-off relocation allowance of €3,000 gross.

## At-will employment

Your employment with Example Engineering GmbH is at will. This means that you or the company may end the employment at any time, with or without cause or notice. Nothing in this letter is a contract for a fixed period of employment.

## Conditions of this offer

This offer depends on:

- your completing Form I-9 and providing documents that show your identity and your authorization to work in the United States, no later than your third day of work
- references that are satisfactory to the company

To accept this offer, please sign and return a copy of this letter by October 30, 2026. We look forward to working with you.

Sincerely,

[For Example Engineering GmbH] [Accepted by the candidate: I accept this offer on the terms set out above.]

Example Engineering GmbH never charges candidates fees."
`;

